{
  "subtype": "faceted_decomposition",
  "concept": "operational_burden",
  "per_column": [
    {
      "name": "primary_impacted_system",
      "is_constitutive_facet": true,
      "role": "facet",
      "rationale": "The affected system/asset is a constitutive aspect of what the operational burden is about -- it characterizes WHERE the burden falls, an intrinsic dimension of the burden itself rather than an external predictor."
    },
    {
      "name": "issue_severity_indicator",
      "is_constitutive_facet": true,
      "role": "facet",
      "rationale": "The nature/severity of the failure (access failure, service unavailable/degraded, config error) is an aspect OF the burden -- it describes what kind of disruption constitutes the burden."
    },
    {
      "name": "scope_of_impact",
      "is_constitutive_facet": true,
      "role": "facet",
      "rationale": "Breadth of impact (individual vs enterprise-wide) is a genuine constitutive dimension of operational burden: how much of the organization the burden weighs on."
    },
    {
      "name": "resolution_complexity_signal",
      "is_constitutive_facet": true,
      "role": "facet",
      "rationale": "The effort/complexity required to resolve is arguably the operational cost dimension of the burden -- an aspect of how burdensome it is to handle, thus a facet of the burden rather than an external cause."
    }
  ],
  "facet_columns": [
    "primary_impacted_system",
    "issue_severity_indicator",
    "scope_of_impact",
    "resolution_complexity_signal"
  ],
  "non_facet_columns": [],
  "mutual_exclusivity": 0.75,
  "exhaustiveness": 0.8,
  "rationale": "All four columns are genuine meronymic facets of operational burden: WHERE it lands (impacted system), WHAT kind of disruption (severity/failure type), HOW BROAD (scope), and HOW COSTLY to resolve (resolution complexity). These carve mostly distinct aspects. Mutual exclusivity is somewhat reduced because issue_severity_indicator and resolution_complexity_signal partially co-vary/overlap: 'service_unavailable/access_failure' severity strongly correlates with and is partly restated by 'routine_access_restore/infrastructure_intervention' resolution categories, so the failure-nature and resolution-effort facets blur together. Exhaustiveness is good but not complete: burden dimensions such as temporal duration/persistence (how long the burden lasts) and volume/frequency (recurrence) of the burden are not captured. Overall a coherent, largely MECE faceted decomposition with minor overlap and a couple of missing constitutive aspects."
}

